<% content_for :title, 'Edit gas giant' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Edit Gas Giant' do %>
  <div class='space-y-8'>
    <p class='text-fg'>
      Manual changes are not validated against the rules in the World Builder's Handbook (WBH). Any value entered here is
      stored as given, so check it against the WBH yourself.
    </p>

    <p class='text-fg'>
      Fields marked with the chip icon are required when adding a gas giant: orbit, period, inclination, eccentricity,
      axial tilt, code and diameter. Mass is optional.
    </p>

    <div>
      <%= render 'application/subsection', title: 'Orbital' %>
      <dl class='mt-4 space-y-5'>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Orbit</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Orbit number around the parent star. The AU distance and orbit sequence are derived from it.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Period</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Orbital period in days.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Rotation</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Sidereal rotation period in hours: the time to turn once relative to the fixed stars (WBH pp. 103&ndash;104).</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Tidally Locked To</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>The body this object keeps the same face towards, chosen from the body it orbits and its star. Leave as Not locked for a freely rotating body (WBH p. 105 onwards).</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Sidereal Day</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Rotation period relative to the stars, in hours (WBH pp. 103&ndash;104). For a tidally locked body this normally matches its orbital period.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Twilight Zone</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Enable if the body is locked so that a narrow habitable band lies between the scorched and frozen hemispheres (WBH p. 105 onwards).</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Tidal Lock Note</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Free text recording how the lock arose or any exceptions, such as a lock that is not complete.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Inclination and Eccentricity</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Inclination in degrees; eccentricity from 0 (circular) upwards.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div>
      <%= render 'application/subsection', title: 'Physical' %>
      <dl class='mt-4 space-y-5'>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Code</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>GS (small), GM (medium) or GL (large).</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Axial tilt</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Tilt of the rotational axis in degrees.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Diameter</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Diameter in kilometres. The jump shadow is derived from it.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Mass</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Mass in solar masses.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
